      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To incorporate neighborhood stability and community cohesion, you could use aggregated public data sources such as local business longevity rates or crime statistics. You might weight these factors using Principal Component Analysis to reduce multicollinearity before integrating them into your risk score. Furthermore, consider proxy metrics like local economic turnover or commercial zoning stability to quantify the environmental risk associated with the business's location. This approach allows you to blend traditional creditworthiness with tangible, localized economic health signals.",
